## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: A department needs a 50GB storage limit, but they want to be warned when they hit 45GB without actually being blocked. How do you configure this?
A1: You configure a "Soft Quota" set to 50GB, and set an email or event log notification threshold at 90% utilization.

Q2: Users are changing the extensions of their `.mp4` files to `.txt` to bypass your File Screen. How does FSRM handle this?
A2: Standard FSRM File Screens only check the file extension, meaning this bypass will successfully trick the server. To stop this, advanced administrators use Active Directory File Classification Infrastructure (FCI) to scan the actual hex headers inside the files, rather than relying purely on the file name.